{"assets":["/statement-assets/c8b53d29b02955ff555f7ec0dceaea76f9cef4fe13c8281e83549af510794688.png","/statement-assets/af572790d886b5de9e6a69678560f5b9ffb802b8d91d49716b2f7199c5afce2c.png","/statement-assets/504f07f758027a6b2e418fe654dd07cab70b19c995ecd454ff0430604defc3ec.png","/statement-assets/69bd9305b2df82da25dc771faa99c625149032ba3b7a6f03d77d2ee53d251cc7.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"645","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"G. Armistice Area Apportionment"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After a drawn-out mooclear arms race, Farmer John and the Mischievous Mess Makers have finally agreed to establish peace. They plan to divide the territory of Bovinia with a line passing through at least two of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" outposts scattered throughout the land. These outposts, remnants of the conflict, are located at the points "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x1, y1), (x2, y2), ..., (xn, yn)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In order to find the optimal dividing line, Farmer John and Elsie have plotted a map of Bovinia on the coordinate plane. Farmer John's farm and the Mischievous Mess Makers' base are located at the points "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"P = (a, 0)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"Q = ( - a, 0)"},{"kind":"text","text":", respectively. Because they seek a lasting peace, Farmer John and Elsie would like to minimize the maximum difference between the distances from any point on the line to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"P"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"Q"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Formally, define the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"difference"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of a line "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/c8b53d29b02955ff555f7ec0dceaea76f9cef4fe13c8281e83549af510794688.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" relative to two points "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"P"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"Q"},{"kind":"text","text":" as the smallest real number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"d"},{"kind":"text","text":" so that for all points "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"X"},{"kind":"text","text":" on line "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/c8b53d29b02955ff555f7ec0dceaea76f9cef4fe13c8281e83549af510794688.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"|PX - QX| ≤ d"},{"kind":"text","text":". (It is guaranteed that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"d"},{"kind":"text","text":" exists and is unique.) They wish to find the line "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/c8b53d29b02955ff555f7ec0dceaea76f9cef4fe13c8281e83549af510794688.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" passing through two distinct outposts "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(xi, yi)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(xj, yj)"},{"kind":"text","text":" such that the difference of "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/c8b53d29b02955ff555f7ec0dceaea76f9cef4fe13c8281e83549af510794688.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" relative to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"P"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"Q"},{"kind":"text","text":" is minimized."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ n ≤ 100 000"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ a ≤ 10 000"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of outposts and the coordinates of the farm and the base, respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The following "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines describe the locations of the outposts as pairs of integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(xi, yi)"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"|xi|, |yi| ≤ 10 000"},{"kind":"text","text":"). These points are distinct from each other as well as from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"P"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"Q"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single real number—the difference of the optimal dividing line. Your answer will be considered correct if its absolute or relative error does not exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10 - 6"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Namely: let's assume that your answer is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the answer of the jury is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":". The checker program will consider your answer correct, if "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/af572790d886b5de9e6a69678560f5b9ffb802b8d91d49716b2f7199c5afce2c.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2 5\n1 0\n2 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"7.2111025509\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 6\n0 1\n2 5\n0 -3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0.0000000000\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample case, the only possible line "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/c8b53d29b02955ff555f7ec0dceaea76f9cef4fe13c8281e83549af510794688.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y = x - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":". It can be shown that the point "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"X"},{"kind":"text","text":" which maximizes "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"|PX - QX|"},{"kind":"text","text":" is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(13, 12)"},{"kind":"text","text":", with "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/504f07f758027a6b2e418fe654dd07cab70b19c995ecd454ff0430604defc3ec.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", which is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/69bd9305b2df82da25dc771faa99c625149032ba3b7a6f03d77d2ee53d251cc7.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample case, if we pick the points "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0, 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0,  - 3)"},{"kind":"text","text":", we get "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/c8b53d29b02955ff555f7ec0dceaea76f9cef4fe13c8281e83549af510794688.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" as "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x = 0"},{"kind":"text","text":". Because "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"PX = QX"},{"kind":"text","text":" on this line, the minimum possible difference is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"G","problemCode":"645G","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/645/problem/G"}